WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:11.400
Tim Caspar: Good morning, welcome. Good morning
and welcome. My name is Timothy Caspar, I

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.090
serve at Hillsdale College as associate vice
president for external affairs. I'm also deputy

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:22.020
editor of Imprimis. I have the privilege of
teaching in the college's, politics department.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.840
I'm a graduate of the college, which was way
back in 1994.

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:33.820
That's starting to seem like a long time ago.
I'll be your emcee for today's program. Welcome

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.360
again to this national leadership seminar.
The constitution and current politics. As

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.260
president Arnn stated so eloquently last night,
there is an important public debate going

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:49.160
on over the meaning of our constitution.
On the one side of the debate, are those who

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:55.460
seek a return to the kind of limited constitutional
of the American founders. I think maybe there

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:02.250
are some of those in this room. On the other
side of the debate, we can place the president,

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:08.749
I hasten to add add of America not of Hillsdale.
The president and his fellow progressive have

00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:13.909
seen no limits to the size of government,
and to what it might accomplish. By the way,

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:19.369
that will take money lots of it. The conservative
news service noted a few days ago that the

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:25.810
federal government has raked in over $1,000,000,000,000.
1,000,000,000,000 of your tax dollars in the

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:32.810
current budget year and still manage to go
200,000,000,000 over budget in the same period.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.069
These progressives are the sorts of folks
that one of my political heroes Ronald Reagan

00:01:38.069 --> 00:01:42.770
had in mind, when he joked, that the 10 most
dangerous words in the English language are,

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:49.639
"Hi, I'm from the government, and I'm here
to help." Reagan was joking as he so often

00:01:49.639 --> 00:01:55.759
did, but he was also making a serious point
as he so often did.

00:01:55.759 --> 00:02:00.600
Americans then and now face the choice between
limited, and unlimited government. As Reagan

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:06.889
put it in his first inaugural or choices between
self-rules were ruled by the so-called experts

00:02:06.889 --> 00:02:12.400
of the administrative state. It's in this
political context that we convene this national

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.610
leadership seminar.
Our first speaker today is Heather Mac Donald.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:23.480
Mrs. Mac Donald is the Thomas W. Smith fellow
at the Manhattan Institute and a contributing

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:30.110
editor of City Journal. She earned her J.D.
at Stanford University Law School and describes

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:35.060
herself as a non-practicing lawyer, I think
we call that a recovering lawyer.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:41.540
She writes about a range of topics including
Homeland Security, Policing and Racial Profiling,

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:46.579
Educational policy and immigration which is
her topic today. Her excellent work has won

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:53.400
her numerous awards, including a 2005 Bradley
Prize. She testifies frequently before congress

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.860
appears quite often on television and writes
from many other publications in addition to

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:03.890
City Journals such as the Wall Street Journal,
Washington Post, National Review, The New

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:09.739
Criterion and many others.
Her book titles include, Are Cops Racist?

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:16.390
How the War Against the Police Harms Black
Americans, and The Immigration Solution. A

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:20.269
better plan than today's which is co-authored
with Hillsdale College distinguish fellow

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:26.620
Victor Davis Hanson, and Steven Malanga. Her
lecture title today is Practical Thoughts

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:31.790
on Immigration. Please welcome Heather Mac
Donald.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:45.220
Heather Mac Donald: Thank you so much this
is an extraordinary honor, and pleasure

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:49.760
to be at the national leadership seminar.
To be out of New York where we're experiencing

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:56.760
a little global cooling this winter. Especially
living in New York, you often forget that

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:02.749
there is people still in America who actually
believe that the founders did a pretty good

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:09.420
job in drafting the constitution and creating
the framework for this country.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.739
To see so many of you here today is quite
heartening and I'm going to bring this memory

00:04:14.739 --> 00:04:21.530
back with me when I go back to the bastion
of the New York Times. President Arnn last

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:29.110
night spoke very dramatically and powerfully
about the constitutional crisis, as he deemed

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:34.840
it, facing conservatives today.
This morning I'm going to speak about one

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:45.800
particular crisis. The lesson from the last
20 years of immigration policy is that lawlessness

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:52.490
breeds more lawlessness. Once a people or
government decides to normalize one form of

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:58.889
law breaking, other forms of lawlessness will
follow until finally the rule of law itself

00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:05.169
is in jeopardy. Last July when I accepted
Mr. Bell's kind invitation to speak to the Hillsdale

00:05:05.169 --> 00:05:11.150
National Leadership Seminar, I had long been
tracking various immigration related assaults

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:17.389
on the rule of law.
I did not foresee that a constitutional crisis

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:25.160
was just on the horizon. President Obama has
decided that because congress has not granted

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:33.860
amnesty to millions of illegal aliens living
in the United States. He will do so himself.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:41.660
Let us ponder for a moment, just how shameless
this assertion of power is.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:46.699
Article 2 section 3 of the constitution says
that, "The President shall take Care that

00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:54.739
the Laws be faithfully executed." That provision
assumes that there is a law for the president

00:05:54.740 --> 00:06:05.320
to execute. In this case, the alleged problem
that Obama is reporting to fix, is the absence

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:10.240
of a law granting amnesty to millions of illegal
aliens.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:17.620
Obama is not executing a law, he's making
one up all by himself. Arrogating to himself

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:25.200
a function that the constitution explicitly
allocates to congress. Should this outrageous

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:32.289
and blatantly unconstitutional power grab
stand we will have moved very far in the direction

00:06:32.289 --> 00:06:38.699
of rule by a dictator-Pace Obama. the absence of a congressional law granting

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:46.559
amnesty is not evidence of a political failure
that he must somehow correct by unilateral

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:54.889
executive action. It is evidence of the lack
of a popular consensus regarding amnesty.

00:06:54.889 --> 00:07:00.280
There has been no amnesty statute because
the political will for such an amnesty is

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:08.660
lacking. Now fortunately on late Monday.
A federal district judge in Texas acknowledged

00:07:08.669 --> 00:07:16.309
this obvious fact, and in a bracing opinion
struck down or put on hold for the moment.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:22.180
Obama's executive amnesty acknowledging the
arguments of half of the states in the country

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:29.440
that this would impose enormous fiscal burdens
on them, but more profoundly that Obama had

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:35.069
violated the constitution.
It's not the end of the story unfortunately.

00:07:35.069 --> 00:07:42.419
This will undoubtedly be appealed to the Fifth
Circuit of appeals in Texas which has recently

00:07:42.419 --> 00:07:48.930
been busily contorting itself into knots,
trying to justify under the constitution racial

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:53.729
preferences, in admissions at the University
of Texas.

00:07:53.729 --> 00:07:59.930
This is not a slam dunk that we have a court
here, that we'll be willing to uphold the

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:10.870
constitution and the congress's prerogative
over immigration matters. For the moment, 

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:17.740
at least this amnesty is on hold. Now Democrats
are assiduously pretending that the Obama

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:26.039
executive amnesty is merely an innocuous exercise
of prosecutorial discretion. If it is ultimately

00:08:26.039 --> 00:08:30.930
upheld by either the 5th Circuit or the Supreme
Court,

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:37.490
they will rue the day that they exceeded
to this travesty, when a Republican president

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:44.860
decides say to privatize social security because
Congress has failed to do so. Now Obama's

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:51.269
executive amnesty is the most public and egregious
example of immigration lawlessness to date.

00:08:51.269 --> 00:08:57.620
Beneath the radar screen has been an equally
telling saga of cascading lawlessness that

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:01.130
is arguably as consequential for our country's
future.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:09.060
I am referring to the attack on the secure
communities program, and on deportation more

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:15.430
generally. I hope to convince you this morning
that because of this attack, the rallying

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:22.430
cry of so many well-meaning conservatives
that we must quote secure the borders is a

00:09:22.459 --> 00:09:28.510
naïve and meaningless delusion.
The secure communities program is a common-

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:34.839
sensical response to illegal alien criminality.
Whenever an illegal alien is booked into a

00:09:34.839 --> 00:09:41.680
local jail for a crime, an alert is automatically
sent to the federal immigration authorities

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:46.589
in the Immigration and Customs of Enforcement
agency or ICE.

00:09:46.589 --> 00:09:51.850
ICE agents can then ask that the jail or
prison briefly hold the illegal alien after

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:58.070
he has served his jail or prison time, rather
than releasing him back into the community,

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:04.510
so that ICE can pick him up to begin deportation
proceedings against him. This is known as

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:12.550
a detainer. You would think that such a program
would be wholly uncontroversial.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:19.230
An alien who crosses into the country illegally
already has no claim to undisturbed presence

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:25.850
here. He is already voluntarily assumed the
risk of deportation. An illegal alien who

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:33.370
then goes on to break other laws, has even
less claim to protection from deportation.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:40.690
Yet, secure communities has been the target
of incessant protest from illegal alien advocates

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:46.310
since its inception.
They make the astonishing claim that it is

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:55.070
unfair to remove an illegal alien who commits
other crimes. Even more astonishing, over

00:10:55.070 --> 00:11:01.829
300 jurisdictions including New York state,
New York City, California, Chicago, and Los

00:11:01.829 --> 00:11:10.500
Angeles agree. They have openly refused to
honor ICE's request for detainers, but instead

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:18.620
have released tens of thousands of criminals back to the
streets, where they easily evade ICE detection.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:23.519
Not that ICE would even think of trying to
pick them up. Indeed the irony regarding secure

00:11:23.519 --> 00:11:30.799
communities is that ICE rarely uses its power
under the program. In 2012, the last year

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:37.389
for which we have complete records. The agency
was notified of over 400,000 illegal alien

00:11:37.389 --> 00:11:46.529
jail detainees but removed only 19% of those.
The removal rate was on track to be even lower

00:11:46.529 --> 00:11:55.669
in 2013. About 50% of those criminal illegal
aliens whom ICE chooses not to deport reoffend

00:11:55.670 --> 00:12:04.070
upon release. There are 2 aspects of the campaign
against secure communities, that bare particular

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:10.850
notice. First the hypocrisy of the Obama Administration
and the advocates.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:20.760
Second the hypocrisy of big city police chiefs.
In 2012, Arizona became the target of universal

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:27.260
contempt among the country's elites for passing
a law that encourage local law enforcement

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:35.360
officers to assist ICE with immigration enforcement.
According to illegal alien advocates and the

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:45.149
Obama Administration, this law known as SB1070
was an unconstitutional state usurpation of

00:12:45.149 --> 00:12:50.870
the federal government's plenary under the
constitution over immigration matters that

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:58.449
includes both congress and the executive branch.
The Obama Administration sued Arizona for

00:12:58.449 --> 00:13:04.720
allegedly interfering with federal authority
over immigration and won in injunction, against

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:14.060
SB1070. It's subsequently been basically gutted.
Yet now, those same advocates are successfully

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:21.660
urging states and localities to defy the federal
government’s request for immigration assistance.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:26.300
Resulting in the creation of local sanctuary
zones where federal immigration authority

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:32.630
cannot reach. If ever there were a lawless
usurpation of the federal government's power

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:41.550
over immigration. The open revolt against
secure communities is it. Yet the Obama Administration

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:49.459
rather than hauling these recalcitrant jurisdictions
to court, has lain supine and is chastely

00:13:49.459 --> 00:13:55.019
looking the other way.
Late last year, it threw in the towel completely

00:13:55.019 --> 00:14:01.269
and dismantled the secure communities program
agreeing with the activist that it was unfair

00:14:01.269 --> 00:14:08.269
to illegal alien criminals to put them under
any worry that they may face the risk of deportation.

00:14:08.269 --> 00:14:12.880
There is another camp aspect of the campaign
against secure communities that shows how

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:18.990
corrosive this tolerance of immigration lawlessness
is.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:25.529
Major police chiefs and immigration jurisdictions
are under enormous political pressure, to

00:14:25.529 --> 00:14:32.220
protect illegal aliens. That has meant tossing
aside everything that they know about public

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:39.019
safety and policing. One of the great insights
of policing over the last 2 decades, was the

00:14:39.019 --> 00:14:44.209
realization that low level misdemeanor offenses
like graffiti, turnstile, jumping, drunk driving,

00:14:44.209 --> 00:14:50.480
and drug sales.
Have an outsize impact on a communities perceptions

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:57.079
of public safety and on the actual reality
of crime. Criminals are rarely scrupulous

00:14:57.079 --> 00:15:04.079
about obeying the law, enforcing misdemeanor
offenses is an effective way of incapacitating

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:11.110
more serious criminals. Even when an offender
just not go on to commit more violent felonies.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:17.550
Such allegedly minor offenses, a shop lifting,
and illegal street vending create a lawlessness

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:22.959
and disorder that breaks down the fabric of
the community.

00:15:22.959 --> 00:15:29.959
Police chiefs like New York William Bratton,
and Los Angeles Charles know this. Yet they

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:36.920
have fiercely opposed cooperating with the
federal government on secure communities on

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:43.649
the ground that misdemeanor offenses are really
too trivial to worry about and should not

00:15:43.649 --> 00:15:50.069
subject in illegal alien to deportation. This
is pure hypocrisy.

00:15:50.069 --> 00:15:56.880
The result of the enormous pressures of demographic
change on our principles. The ultimate goal

00:15:56.880 --> 00:16:03.880
of the secure communities program is to de-illegitimate
deportation entirely as a response to illegal

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:10.940
immigration. If it is morally unacceptable
to deport even a convicted illegal alien criminal,

00:16:11.529 --> 00:16:18.529
then it is all the more unacceptable to deport
someone who is merely cross the border illegally.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:25.610
The undermining of deportation is behind those
constant protest demanding in the words of

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:32.610
the protesters to end deportations now. It
is behind the claim that it is Americans who

00:16:34.279 --> 00:16:40.470
are to blame for separating families, rather
than the alien annoyingly came into the country

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:47.139
in violation of our immigration laws, and
assume the risk of being sent home.

00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:53.040
The campaign against deportation does not
name itself as such, but it is been highly

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:57.889
successful. Despite the false rhetoric of
the Obama Administration. Deportation has

00:16:57.889 --> 00:17:04.889
basically disappeared from the interior of
the country. The removal rate in 2014, for

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:11.940
illegal aliens who are not explicit ICE priorities
was .05%.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:20.220
What's the consequence of eliminating deportation
as a response to illegal immigration. If someone

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:27.390
cannot be removed for illegal entry, then
there is no more immigration law. Deportation

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:34.590
is the only remedy for illegal entry that
actually corrects and deters the original

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:39.650
law-breaking.
For that reason, Mexico, and every other country

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:46.650
on earth practices it. Even if the activist
would accept a fine as a penalty for illegal

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:54.670
entry and that's not at all clear. That fine
simply becomes the cost of entering. Lose

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:59.800
deportation as we're doing, and the United
States will formally ceded control of its

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:05.680
immigration policy to people living outside
the borders. National sovereignty will become

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:10.610
meaningless, and formal immigration policy
a nullity.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:15.870
The de-legitimization of deportation is why
the conservative rallying cry to secure the

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:22.870
borders is so naïve. An utterly secure border
is impossible, people will always find a way

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:30.510
to cross, but if once they cross nothing can
be done to them, then we may as well not have

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:35.880
any borders at all.
That's why the advocates have spent all their

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:42.420
energy fighting deportation rather than fighting
increase border security because they know

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:49.420
that eradicating the former, is far more important.
Now the erosion of the rule is bad enough,

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:56.830
but the social consequence of these mass illegal
immigration is equally troubling.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:05.140
We were importing poverty and educational
failure. If you want to see America's future,

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:09.520
look no further than my home state of California
which is a generation ahead of the rest of

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:16.310
the country and experiencing the effects of
unchecked immigration from the South. Nearly

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:23.310
50% of all California births are now Hispanic.
The state Hispanic population is now almost

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:30.150
equal to the white population and it's school
population is vastly majority Hispanic. The

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:36.550
consequences of this demographic shift have
been profound. In the 1950s and 1960s California

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:43.550
led in educational achievement. Today with
majority Hispanic K-12 population.

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:49.790
The largest concentration of English language
learners in the country. California is at

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:56.230
the bottom of the educational HEAP. Barely
distinguishable in its national test scores

00:19:56.230 --> 00:20:03.230
from such economic backwaters as Mississippi,
Alabama and Louisiana. Over a third of California

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:08.380
8th graders lack even the most rudimentary
Math skills.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:14.670
28% are equally deficient in reading. The
mathematics performance gap between Hispanic

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:21.670
and white 8th graders is not budge since 1990.
The reading gap has improved only slightly

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:28.920
since 1998. California is at the epicenter
of a disturbing phenomenon known as long term

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:34.130
English Language Learners.
You would think that an English Learner would

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:39.870
be somebody who grew up in a foreign country,
speaking a foreign language who came to the

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:46.870
US only later in life. In fact the vast majority
of designated English learners are born here.

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:54.710
Their cognitive and language skills are so
low that they're deemed non-native English

00:20:54.710 --> 00:21:01.710
speakers. Nationally 30% of all English Language
Learners are 3rd generation Americans.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:12.760
There's a problem of a simulation going on.
In 2013, California governor Jerry Brown push

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:20.810
through a controversial law to try to close
the achievement gap in California. Between

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:27.140
California's growing Hispanic population and
it's Anglo and Asian populations. That law

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:32.540
redistributes tax dollars from successful
schools to those with high proportions of

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:38.070
English learners and low income students.
It remains to be seen whether these latest

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:43.780
effort to raise the education outcomes of
these children of low skilled immigrants will

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:49.670
prove more effective than its predecessors
working against that possibility is Hispanic's

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:55.960
high dropout rate, the highest of any group
in the nation, and they're equally unmatched

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:02.560
teen pregnancy rate.
To be sure many illegal Hispanics who come

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:09.560
here possess admirable work ethic, one that
American should emulate. Some have turned

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:16.730
around very troubled in our city communities
like South Central LA or at least have started

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:23.300
them on an upward trajectory. Thanks to their
lack of social capital.

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:29.730
Many of their children and grandchildren are
getting sacked up into underclass culture.

00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:36.730
The Hispanic out of wedlock birth rate in
California and the US is 53%. Twice what it

00:22:37.770 --> 00:22:44.770
was when the black population in 1965. When
Daniel Patrick Moynihan wrote his present

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:50.670
warning about the catastrophe of black family
breakdown.

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:57.670
In 65 it was 23% for blacks, and as Larry
Kudlow said last night, Moynihan was travestied

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:07.110
as a racist but he was utterly farseeing in
his observation that a 23% illegitimacy rate

00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:16.130
was probab- Hispanics are now up to 53% twice
as much. The incarceration rate of Mexican-Americans

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:25.100
in California shoots up 8 times between the
first and second generation to equal the black

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:30.620
incarceration rate.
Gang involvement is endemic in barrio schools,

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:36.200
I wish I could take some of my fellow open
borders conservatives to the Berrendo Middle

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:42.930
School, in Pico Rivera in Los Angeles where
I've spent time. They would see a massive

00:23:42.930 --> 00:23:49.930
social service bureaucracy of anti-gang councilors
serving the children of single mothers.

